    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45-a5">

                <pb facs="0099" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg89"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 13, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 11th instant, and its enclosures, respecting the alleged
                    engagement of seamen at Liverpool for the service of the so-styled Confederate
                    States, and I have to inform you that I have lost no time in forwarding your
                    letter to the proper department of her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
